# Gate step — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq). Wired by 1087-h2z9.
#
# Triaged from scripts/gate-divergence-declared.txt, where it sat `untriaged`
# since 2026-09-06: present in --ci-full, absent from --check, nobody decided.
# Measured green and cheap on b026372ff (Cheatsheet references), so the honest verdict is to run
# it where every host lands rather than once a day on the release gate.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf): a binding assembled
# from a variable is invisible to every name-based scan.
STEP_DESC="Checking cheatsheet references resolve"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/check-cheatsheet-refs.lua"
STEP_ERROR="a cheatsheet reference does not resolve (1087-h2z9)"
STEP_OK="Cheatsheet references passed"

# NO STEP_SKIP_EXIT ANY MORE (1570-k4fx). The .sh this step ran exited 2 when
# ripgrep was available neither on the host nor in the tillandsias-builder
# toolbox, and that nomination kept the tooling gap from refusing a land as a
# content verdict about zero references (esmeraldinha 2026-09-12, WSL2, no rg,
# LAND_EXIT=3). The Lua port reads the files itself and needs no tool, so there
# is no could-not-run condition left to nominate; its only exit 2 is a missing
# cheatsheets/ directory, which is a broken checkout and must refuse, not skip.
# The STEP_SKIP_EXIT mechanism itself stays pinned by
# scripts/test-gate-step-skip-exit.sh against a stub subject.
#
# The second-regime record below was taken on the .sh; the port has not yet
# been run on darwin or msys (pure fs reads, no spawn: an argument, not a
# measurement).
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="macneo 2026-09-22 darwin ok:rc0-no-verdict-line"
